# VK access token (home daily indexer)

- Production VK calls for `users.search` / daily index use a **classic `vk1.a` user token**.
- The token is **IP-bound to the home PC** and typically lasts **~24h** (no reliable offline scope).
- **Never** invent tokens, paste from chat history, or use VK ID `vk2.a` for indexing.

## Canonical renew URL (mandatory)

Always obtain a fresh token **only** from this exact authorize URL (Cursor IDE browser, with the user's existing VK session):

```
https://oauth.vk.com/authorize?client_id=54762499&display=page&redirect_uri=https://oauth.vk.com/blank.html&response_type=token&v=5.199
```

Do not substitute another `client_id`, add `scope=offline`, or use `id.vk.com` / PKCE for the indexer token.

## Agent procedure

1. Open that URL in the Cursor browser (`browser_navigate`).
2. After redirect to `oauth.vk.com/blank.html#access_token=vk1.a...` (or `oauth.vk.ru/blank.html#...`), read the **full** address bar / page URL.
3. Save via `scripts/_vk-save-classic.sh` (write URL into `/tmp/fg-vk-classic-url.txt` first) — this updates VPS `/opt/fitnessgirl-meet/.env` `VK_ACCESS_TOKEN`.
4. Verify from home: `bash scripts/_probe-vk-from-home.sh` (`users.get` must succeed).

## When to renew

- Before any daily index if probe fails (expired / invalid / wrong IP).
- Proactively when the user asks to run daily index and the token is near expiry.
- **Every day ~23:00** Windows task `FitnessgirlVkTokenRenewCheck` probes the token. If dead it writes `~/fg-logs/vk-needs-renew.flag`, opens the canonical OAuth URL, and toasts the user — when you see that (or the flag), **renew immediately** in Cursor browser so 00:00 daily index can run.
- Do **not** ask the user to copy the token if the Cursor browser VK session works — renew yourself.

## Marker file

If `~/fg-logs/vk-needs-renew.flag` (or `%USERPROFILE%\fg-logs\vk-needs-renew.flag`) exists, treat renew as urgent and clear the flag only after a successful `vk-renew-classic.sh` + probe.
